    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1757">

                <pb facs="1146" n="1030" xml:id="pg1030"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.77/173.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Price.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 7, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Consult freely with Colonel Goethals and discuss with him all details of the
                    Hebard railway contract. You should bear in mind that the three points to which
                    the Department objects are (1) contravention of Article 5 of the Canal
                    Convention (2) features objectionable from military standpoint (3) pledging
                    annuity of $250,000 or income from six million dollars permanently invested.</p>
                <p>Report fully, by cable, if necessary, conclusions reached at this conference.</p>
                <p>Department desires duplicate copies with translations of proposed contract with
                    Hebard and Company. State if this is ad referendum.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
